    "last_assistant_text": "The PoC triggered the vulnerability successfully on the first attempt. The ASAN output confirms the exact crash: heap-buffer-overflow READ of size 1 at `g_utf8_casefold` in `guniprop.c:1170`, with the 2-byte region `[0x602000000070, 0x602000000072)` being the `g_strndup`'d buffer containing `[0xC0, 0x00]`.\n\nThe single byte `0xC0` triggers the bug because:\n1. `g_strndup` allocates a 2-byte heap buffer `[0xC0, 0x00]`\n2. `g_utf8_casefold` loops while `*p != 0` — the `0xC0` byte passes this check\n3. `g_utf8_next_char(p)` uses `g_utf8_skip[0xC0] = 2` to advance `p` by 2 bytes, skipping past the NUL terminator\n4. The next `*p` dereference in the `while` condition reads 1 byte past the end of the heap buffer",
